<style>
.ahd{margin-bottom:24px}.ameta{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin-bottom:12px;flex-wrap:wrap}
.atg{font-size:11px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.5px;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:4px}
.adt{font-size:12px;color:var(--g4)}
.atit{font-size:clamp(24px,4vw,36px);font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.8px;line-height:1.18;margin-bottom:12px}
.atit em{font-style:normal;color:var(--acc)}
.aint{font-size:16px;color:var(--g3);line-height:1.8;border-left:3px solid var(--acc);padding-left:16px}
.calc{margin:20px 0;border:2px solid var(--acc);border-radius:var(--rl);overflow:hidden}
.cah{background:var(--acc);padding:13px 18px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;color:#fff}
.cah svg{width:18px;height:18px;flex-shrink:0}
.cat{font-size:14px;font-weight:600}.cas{font-size:12px;opacity:.85}
.cab{padding:18px;background:#fff}
.caf{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px;margin-bottom:14px}
.cal{font-size:11px;font-weight:600;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.4px;color:var(--g4);margin-bottom:5px}
.cas2{width:100%;height:37px;padding:0 10px;border:1.5px solid var(--g5);border-radius:8px;font-size:13px;font-family:var(--f);background:var(--wh);outline:none;transition:border-color .15s;appearance:none}
.cas2:focus{border-color:var(--acc)}
.cai{width:100%;height:37px;padding:0 10px;border:1.5px solid var(--g5);border-radius:8px;font-size:13px;font-family:var(--m);background:var(--wh);outline:none;transition:border-color .15s;margin-bottom:14px;display:block}
.cai:focus{border-color:var(--acc)}
.cpre{display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:12px}
.cpr{padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--g5);border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;color:var(--g4);cursor:pointer;background:var(--wh);font-family:var(--f);transition:all .12s}
.cpr:hover,.cpr.on{border-color:var(--acc);color:var(--acd);background:var(--acl)}
.cbtn{width:100%;height:42px;background:var(--acc);color:#fff;border:none;border-radius:9px;font-size:14px;font-weight:500;cursor:pointer;font-family:var(--f);transition:background .15s}
.cbtn:hover{background:var(--acd)}
.cres{margin-top:16px;display:none}.cres.show{display:block}
.crt{font-size:11px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.5px;color:var(--g4);margin-bottom:9px}
.crw{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:7px}
.crr{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:10px 13px;border:1px solid var(--g5);border-radius:9px}
.crr.best{border:1.5px solid var(--acc);background:var(--acl)}
.crl{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px}
.crd{width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;flex-shrink:0}
.df{background:var(--acc)}.dm{background:var(--am)}.ds{background:var(--g4)}
.crn{font-size:13px;font-weight:500}.crt2{font-size:11px;color:var(--g4);margin-top:1px}
.crp{font-size:15px;font-weight:700;font-family:var(--m)}
.crr.best .crp{color:var(--acd)}
.cbtg{font-size:10px;font-weight:700;background:var(--acc);color:#fff;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:4px;text-transform:uppercase;margin-left:4px}
.cdis{font-size:11px;color:var(--g4);margin-top:8px;line-height:1.6}
.lg{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(180px,1fr));gap:11px;margin:14px 0 22px}
.lc{border:1px solid var(--g5);border-radius:var(--rl);padding:13px;transition:border-color .15s}
.lc:hover{border-color:var(--acc)}.lc.rec{border:2px solid var(--acc)}
.lbg{font-size:10px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.4px;padding:2px 7px;border-radius:4px;display:inline-block;margin-bottom:7px}
.lbf{background:var(--acl);color:var(--acd)}.lbv{background:var(--gnl);color:var(--gn)}.lbb{background:var(--g6);color:var(--g4)}
.lbm{background:var(--pul);color:var(--pu)}
.ln{font-size:13.5px;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:3px}.lt{font-size:11.5px;color:var(--g4);margin-bottom:9px}
.lstat{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px}
.lsr{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:12px}
.lsr span:first-child{color:var(--g4)}.lsr span:last-child{font-family:var(--m);font-weight:500}
.tw{overflow-x:auto;margin:14px 0 22px;border:1px solid var(--g5);border-radius:var(--rl)}
.tw table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px;min-width:540px}
.tw th{padding:9px 13px;text-align:left;background:var(--g6);font-size:11px;font-weight:600;color:var(--g4);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.4px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--g5)}
.tw td{padding:9px 13px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--g5);color:var(--g2);vertical-align:middle}
.tw tr:last-child td{border-bottom:none}.tw tr:hover td{background:var(--g6)}
.tf{color:var(--acc);font-weight:500}.tm{color:var(--am);font-weight:500}.ts{color:var(--g4)}
.mv{font-family:var(--m);font-size:12px}
.sbsr{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;padding:6px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--g5);font-size:13px}
.sbsr span:first-child{color:var(--g3)}.sbsr span:last-child{font-family:var(--m);font-weight:500;font-size:12px}
@media(max-width:599px){.caf{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
 
<div class="pw">
<main class="fade-in">
  <header class="ahd">
    <div class="ameta">
      <span class="atg" style="background:var(--acl);color:var(--acd)">Shipping Guide</span>
      <span class="adt">Updated June 2026</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="atit">USFans shipping to the UK<br><em>Royal Mail · HMRC · times 2026</em></h1>
    <p class="aint">Ship to the United Kingdom after QC: compare lines, delivery windows, and real costs. Last-mile is often <strong>Royal Mail</strong>; duties follow <strong>HMRC</strong>. Northern Ireland is often another SKU. Brand spreadsheet stays on <a href="https://usfansspreadsheet.net/">usfansspreadsheet.net</a>.</p>
  <p class="hub-uplink" data-uk-deepen="20261027" data-step4-hub="1">Brand / Spreadsheet / Coupons truth → <a href="https://usfansspreadsheet.net/">usfansspreadsheet.net</a> · <a href="https://usfansspreadsheet.net/usfans-coupons/">coupons</a> · <a href="https://usfansspreadsheet.net/usfans-spreadsheet/">spreadsheet</a> (Independent Index · 10,601). This URL = UK local (HMRC / Royal Mail / UK postcode / NI). Twin <code>usfansspreadsheet.uk</code> stays 301 → <code>.co.uk</code> — not revived.</p>
  </header>
  
<section id="local" class="local-box" data-uk-fingerprint="hmrc-royal-mail-ni" data-uk-deepen="20261027">
<h2>UK fingerprint before you book a line</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Estimator destination: United Kingdom (GB)</strong> — not this TLD, not EU, not IE.</li>
<li><strong>Address</strong> — UK postcode. <strong>Northern Ireland</strong> is often another carrier product; do not assume the same Royal Mail SKU as mainland GB.</li>
<li><strong>Last mile</strong> — often <strong>Royal Mail</strong> (or the live SKU handoff). Quiet gaps between export and first UK scan are common on economy air.</li>
<li><strong>Duties / VAT</strong> — the booked SKU decides prepaid vs collect. Source the morning you ship: <a href="https://www.gov.uk/goods-sent-from-abroad" rel="noopener" target="_blank">HMRC goods sent from abroad</a>. No declared-value coaching on this desk.</li>
</ol>
<p>Also: <a href="/usfans-refund-guide/">UK refunds</a> · <a href="/usfans-freight/">freight / customs notes</a> · hub spreadsheet on <a href="https://usfansspreadsheet.net/">.net</a>.</p>
</section>

  <h2 class="ph" id="calculator">Free USFans shipping calculator</h2>
  <div class="calc" id="calc">
    <div class="cah">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><rect x="2" y="3" width="20" height="14" rx="2"/><line x1="8" y1="21" x2="16" y2="21"/><line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12" y2="21"/></svg>
      <div><p class="cat">USFans Shipping Calculator</p><p class="cas">Estimates based on 2026 rate tables</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="cab">
      <div class="caf">
        <div><p class="cal">Destination</p>
          <select class="cas2" id="cc" onchange="cu()">
            <option value="us">&#127482;&#127480; United States</option>
            <option value="uk">&#127468;&#127463; United Kingdom</option>
            <option value="au">&#127462;&#127482; Australia</option>
            <option value="ca">&#127464;&#127462; Canada</option>
            <option value="de">&#127465;&#127466; Germany</option>
            <option value="fr">&#127467;&#127479; France</option>
            <option value="jp">&#127471;&#127477; Japan</option>
            <option value="sg">&#127480;&#127468; Singapore</option>
            <option value="br">&#127463;&#127479; Brazil</option>
            <option value="other">&#127757; Other</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div><p class="cal">Item category</p>
          <select class="cas2" id="ccat" onchange="cc2()">
            <option value="shoes">Shoes / Sneakers</option>
            <option value="clothing">Clothing (T-shirt)</option>
            <option value="jacket">Jacket / Coat</option>
            <option value="bag">Bag / Backpack</option>
            <option value="accessories">Accessories</option>
            <option value="custom">Custom weight &darr;</option>
          </select>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="cal" style="margin-bottom:7px">Quick presets</p>
      <div class="cpre" id="cpre">
        <button class="cpr" onclick="sw2(300)">300g &mdash; tee</button>
        <button class="cpr on" onclick="sw2(700)">700g &mdash; shoes</button>
        <button class="cpr" onclick="sw2(1200)">1.2kg &mdash; jacket</button>
        <button class="cpr" onclick="sw2(2000)">2kg &mdash; bag</button>
      </div>
      <p class="cal" style="margin-bottom:5px">Weight (grams)</p>
      <input type="number" class="cai" id="cw" value="700" min="100" max="30000" step="50" oninput="cu()">
      <button class="cbtn" onclick="cu(true)">Calculate shipping cost &rarr;</button>
      <div class="cres" id="cres">
        <p class="crt">Estimated shipping options</p>
        <div class="crw" id="crow"></div>
        <p class="cdis">* Estimates only &mdash; actual rates may vary &plusmn;10%. Domestic freight ($1&ndash;3) not included.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <h2 class="ph">All USFans shipping lines</h2>
  <div class="lg">
    <div class="lc rec"><span class="lbg lbf">Fastest</span><p class="ln">DHL Express</p><p class="lt">5&ndash;8 days to USA</p><div class="lstat"><div class="lsr"><span>700g &rarr; USA</span><span>~$38</span></div><div class="lsr"><span>Tracking</span><span>Full</span></div></div></div>
    <div class="lc"><span class="lbg lbm">Balanced</span><p class="ln">EMS</p><p class="lt">10&ndash;20 days to USA</p><div class="lstat"><div class="lsr"><span>700g &rarr; USA</span><span>~$24</span></div><div class="lsr"><span>Tracking</span><span>Full</span></div></div></div>
    <div class="lc"><span class="lbg lbv">Best value</span><p class="ln">Economy Line A</p><p class="lt">15&ndash;25 days to USA</p><div class="lstat"><div class="lsr"><span>700g &rarr; USA</span><span>~$16</span></div><div class="lsr"><span>Tracking</span><span>Partial</span></div></div></div>
    <div class="lc"><span class="lbg lbb">Slowest</span><p class="ln">Economy Line B</p><p class="lt">25&ndash;45 days to USA</p><div class="lstat"><div class="lsr"><span>700g &rarr; USA</span><span>~$11</span></div><div class="lsr"><span>Tracking</span><span>Limited</span></div></div></div>
  </div>
  
<section class="uk-thicken" id="ship-to-uk" data-uk-deepen="20261027">
<h2>Does USFans ship to the UK — and how long?</h2>
<p>Yes: pick destination <strong>United Kingdom (GB)</strong> in the official estimator after QC. Shoppers asking <em>does usfans ship to uk</em> or <em>how long does usfans take to ship to uk</em> need line choice + last-mile reality — not a second spreadsheet hub.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Typical air window</strong> — express lines often land faster; economy air adds quiet days before the first <strong>Royal Mail</strong> (or live SKU) scan. Re-read the calculator table the morning you pay freight.</li>
<li><strong>HMRC buffer</strong> — budget import VAT/duty separately from the freight quote. Prepaid vs collect is on the SKU; this desk never invents a threshold.</li>
<li><strong>Northern Ireland</strong> — confirm the live product; NI is frequently not the same Royal Mail mainland SKU.</li>
<li><strong>Tracking gaps</strong> — export → customs → UK scan can stall; wait for a carrier event before a missing-parcel ticket unless the SLA in-app says otherwise.</li>
</ul>
<p>Refunds after a failed delivery: <a href="/usfans-refund-guide/">refund guide</a>. Brand finds index: <a href="https://usfansspreadsheet.net/usfans-spreadsheet/">hub spreadsheet</a>.</p>
</section>

  <h2 class="ph">Delivery times by country</h2>
  <div class="tw"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Country</th><th>DHL Express</th><th>EMS</th><th>Economy A</th><th>Economy B</th><th>DHL cost (700g)</th></tr></thead>
